**Root cause:** Every test follows the same anti-pattern — call the method to touch coverage lines, then either assert nothing or assert `IsNotNull`. This inflates line coverage to ~95% while verifying almost zero business logic. The fix is to replace every `IsNotNull` / missing-assert with value-level assertions (`AreEqual`) and add negative-path tests.
